1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,066
A guarded aerospace site.

2
00:00:02,435 --> 00:00:08,370
A drone heads for it, confirmed about nine
hundred and fifty metres out: in time for

3
00:00:08,370 --> 00:00:09,289
the operator.

4
00:00:09,659 --> 00:00:12,837
What should the screen say when no sensor
sees it?

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:16,762
MoVi gives every track one of three
answers.

6
00:00:17,082 --> 00:00:18,035
I see it.

7
00:00:18,355 --> 00:00:20,672
I don't see it: here is where it can be.

8
00:00:20,991 --> 00:00:22,198
Or: I don't know.

9
00:00:22,517 --> 00:00:24,912
It says empty only where it has looked.

10
00:00:25,232 --> 00:00:30,297
A possible-presence warning stays on until
the whole zone is looked at, or the object

11
00:00:30,297 --> 00:00:31,131
is seen again.

12
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:43,290
Radar, LiDAR, cameras, and what aircraft
and drones broadcast: all simulated from

13
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:44,672
public data sheets.

14
00:00:45,019 --> 00:00:49,141
Where a sensor cannot see a drone, the
zone stays unverified.

15
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,311
Dense fog.

16
00:00:52,616 --> 00:00:54,846
MoVi declares each sensor's reach.

17
00:00:55,151 --> 00:00:59,937
For a small drone, the radar's range drops
from one thousand and sixty-two to one

18
00:00:59,937 --> 00:01:04,428
thousand and forty-one metres: a small
change, and not an independent check.

19
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,535
Two drones collide.

20
00:01:11,875 --> 00:01:17,725
MoVi infers contact two point two seconds
later; within two seconds in fifty-one

21
00:01:17,725 --> 00:01:18,748
runs of sixty.

22
00:01:19,088 --> 00:01:20,889
A debris zone opens.

23
00:01:21,229 --> 00:01:25,452
It grows, does not shrink by looking, and
cannot tell who is at risk.

24
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,632
An engine fails on the take-off run, with
a flash.

25
00:01:33,952 --> 00:01:39,242
MoVi declares the blinded cameras
unreliable, within three cycles in every

26
00:01:39,242 --> 00:01:40,242
simulated run.

27
00:01:40,562 --> 00:01:45,669
Only the radar is left: in this run it
loses the aircraft for seconds at a time,

28
00:01:45,669 --> 00:01:46,755
and MoVi says so.

29
00:01:47,074 --> 00:01:51,222
The debris warning does not discriminate:
about ninety-six tracks.

30
00:01:54,210 --> 00:01:55,574
First, the limits.

31
00:01:55,923 --> 00:02:00,080
All simulated from public data sheets: no
physical sensor.

32
00:02:00,429 --> 00:02:03,136
Almost half the values are assumed.

33
00:02:03,486 --> 00:02:05,746
Classes are labelled by hand.

34
00:02:06,095 --> 00:02:09,249
For aircraft in flight, warnings come too
late.

35
00:02:09,599 --> 00:02:14,352
A drone that stops can slip out of the
warning: twelve runs of two hundred.

36
00:02:14,702 --> 00:02:20,198
What holds, in simulation: a drone on the
site was announced in time in two hundred

37
00:02:20,198 --> 00:02:25,297
runs of two hundred, and its position
never declared empty, with the site map

38
00:02:25,297 --> 00:02:26,489
declared complete.

39
00:02:29,710 --> 00:02:35,667
The core comes from our short-range
version: a person behind an obstacle, a

40
00:02:35,667 --> 00:02:38,606
depth camera, the same three answers.

41
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:40,636
MoVi.

42
00:02:40,927 --> 00:02:43,871
Seen, not seen, unknown: declared for
every track.

43
00:02:44,161 --> 00:02:45,881
It observes and warns.

44
00:02:46,172 --> 00:02:47,944
No output is a command.

45
00:02:48,235 --> 00:02:49,849
By SDMs.
